# Line endings.
#
# Added after a concrete failure: the lab GPU machine writes CRLF, a Linux
# checkout with core.autocrlf=input has LF, and results/run_manifest.json records
# the sha256 of every artifact. 28 tracked JSON/CSV files that were byte-identical
# in git therefore hashed differently on the two machines and were reported as
# integrity failures. The hashing side now normalises text before hashing, but the
# root cause is that the two working trees genuinely differed -- this file fixes
# that, so the two agree in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these. A newline substitution inside model weights or a
# dataset is corruption, and must be visible as corruption rather than silently
# "normalised".
*.onnx  binary
*.pt    binary
*.npz   binary
*.npy   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico   binary
